=== SURVEY ===
File: internal/database/signal_history_writer.go (345 lines before changes)
Existing methods: Append, FlushLoop, flush, Cleanup, GetHistory, GetGlobalStats,
  Query, AvailableSignals, GetLatestPerSignal, Stats
Struct: SignalHistoryWriter { db *DB, mu sync.Mutex, buffer []SignalHistoryRow, interval time.Duration }
Table indexes: idx_signal_history_vehicle_signal_time (vehicle_id, signal, created_at DESC)
Dependency: phase-12-00 (hypertable) — DONE per done.txt

=== REASONING ===
1. SnapshotAt — nearly identical to GetLatestPerSignal but adds `created_at <= $2` filter.
   DISTINCT ON (signal) ORDER BY signal, created_at DESC is optimal with the composite index.
   Also selects created_at column (useful for callers who need to know data freshness).
2. SignalAt — single-signal lookup. Uses ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1 instead of
   DISTINCT ON; returns nil (not error) when pgx.ErrNoRows.
3. SnapshotBetween — same as SnapshotAt but with `created_at >= $2 AND created_at <= $3`.
   Gives "what changed during this window" semantics.
All three methods:
- Use 10s context.WithTimeout to prevent runaway scans
- Return empty map/nil (not nil map) when no data found
- Wrap errors with fmt.Errorf for context
- Are read-only (no writes, no mutations)
- Match existing code style (scan into pointers, switch on non-nil)

=== CHANGES ===
